###Setting up a proportion

Corresponding sides of similar triangles are proportional, so we can set up and solve a proportion:

$\dfrac{AB}{AC}=\dfrac{CA}{DA}$

Side $\overline{AB}$ is equal to $\blueE{\overline{BD}}+\overline{DA}$ and we need to find the length of $\blueE{\overline{BD}}$.

We picked side $\overline{AC}$ because it corresponds to side $\overline{AB}$.

Then we picked another pair of corresponding sides where we already knew the measurements.

$\begin{array}{rcl}
&\triangle CAB
\\
{\text{hypotenuse}}
&\overbrace{\underbrace{\!\!\!\!\!\left\{ 
\dfrac{\blueE{BD}+DA}{AC}=\dfrac{CA}{DA}
\right\}\!\!\!\!\!}}
&{\text{long} \atop \text{leg}}
\\
&\triangle DAC
\end{array}$
